cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scQC in your work, please cite it."
title: "scQC: a reproducible quality-control pipeline for single-cell and single-nuclei RNA-seq"
abstract: >-
  scQC separates deriving quality-control thresholds from applying them. Each parameter in
  its report's parameter table carries a class recording whether it was fixed by the pipeline,
  derived from the data, declared in advance, or adjudicated by a human, and every removal is
  recorded with its criteria and remains recoverable. Thresholds that can be measured are
  measured per cohort rather than transferred. On nuclei the count floors come from the density
  valley between the debris and cell modes; on whole cells, where the floors are declared, the
  multiple of the mitochondrial ceiling comes from the cohort's own Tukey fences. On both the
  ceiling is set per library from its own dispersion. Checks that a loss has fallen unevenly
  across the arms of the experimental design run at the ambient, cell-call and doublet steps.
